From: j7 fb
Subject: j7 fb: replace wide black runs, and split the copy timing

The alpha test settled the wallpaper question: a whole frame carried only 4320 fully 
transparent pixels, so the desktop is not sent as transparency and there is no second layer 
to composite. It arrives as opaque black. Replace wide runs of opaque black instead - a 
wallpaper area is hundreds of pixels across and a glyph stem is one or two - so text and 
icons survive.

The paired stores did not move the 34 ms copy, so stop guessing: time the row build and the 
panel stores separately and print both.

Co-Authored-By: dipa-studio <183933817+dipa-studio@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
